  "question": {
    "text": "An LCR circuit as shown in the figure is connected to a voltage source $\\mathrm{V}_{\\mathrm{ac}}$ whose frequency can be varied.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/aMUN3q9hjrgt0pbKw-d5lIVIkxwfEwHbjoBB6qCecME.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\nThe frequency, at which the voltage across the resistor is maximum, is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AcbEF",
      "text": "\n$902 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "ls128",
      "text": "\n$143 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lCF50",
      "text": "\n$23 \\mathrm{~Hz}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "RX9Mr",
      "text": "\n$345 \\mathrm{~Hz}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Frequency $\\mathrm{f}=\\frac{1}{2 \\pi \\sqrt{\\mathrm{LC}}}$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\frac{1}{2 \\times 3.4 \\sqrt{24 \\times 2 \\times 10^{-6}}} \\\\\n& \\simeq 23 \\mathrm{~Hz}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
